I’m pleased to share my Meta Ad Performance Analysis project developed in Microsoft Power BI, designed to provide campaign-level visibility and actionable insights for digital advertising teams.

Project overview

Developed an interactive dashboard to track impressions, clicks, engagements, conversions, and spend across campaigns, ad types, and audience segments (age, gender, country).

Implemented granular time and event-level analysis (day of week, week number, time of day) to identify peak engagement windows and conversion patterns.

Created a semantic data model linking campaigns, ads, users, and ad events for flexible slicing and drill-through analysis.

Key metrics surfaced

Impressions: 57.2K • Clicks: 6.8K • Engagements: 7.8K

Shares: 344 • Comments: 699 • Purchases: 335

CTR: 11.88% • Engagement Rate: 13.70% • Conversion Rate: 4.93%

Total Budget: $2.5M • Avg Budget per Campaign: $50.7K

Tools & techniques

Power BI: report design, bookmarks, slicers, maps, and KPI tiles

Power Query: ETL, timestamp parsing, and event unification

Data modeling: star schema linking campaigns, ads, users, ad_events, and calendar table

DAX: calculated measures for CTR, conversion/purchase rate, and engagement metrics

Analysis: cohort/time-series, audience segmentation, campaign & ad-type performance tables

Impact / Use cases

Prioritized campaigns and ad formats by ROAS-style signals (engagement → conversion)

Identified high-converting days/times and top-performing audience segments for budget reallocation

Enabled stakeholders to run ad-level diagnostics and make evidence-based strategic decisions
